There are demonstrations of creating designs for study areas with multiple strata in Chapter 3 of the Distance for Windows Users Guide.  It is example 4, that provides step-by-step instructions, the first page of which looks like this

Following those instructions and importing the shape files provided with Distance for Windows in the Sample Projects folder (as described in the Users Guide), you can produce a shape file with four strata (from northern Mexico) in your Distance for Windows window, looking something like this:

I have highlighted the strata boundaries as they are a bit difficult to see against the blue background.

An exercise similar to this, based around this Mexico study area is presented (and narrated) in our online workshop materials, Chapter 4. Link below.

https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/
