Hello again,

During modelling i ran into a problem regarding hotspot locations in my datasets. I ustilised the transect line sampling for calculating the feral pigeon population size. But now i seem to run into the problem of hotspot locations in my datasets.

In one of the areas there are dovetils which are hotspots for feral pigeons and high numbers are recorded there. But this means that there will be spikes in the dataset around this hotspot location. Like the graph below:

When applying the models in R the models don't give warnings and visually fit the data. But when i check the goodness of fit they are always significant when a hotspot was present in the area.

Is there a possible way to change the dataset and incorporate them so i have non-significant models or should I select the visually best fitting model and utilize that model to generate my data even though it's goodness of fit is significant?

With kind regards,

Casolyn

