Sudip

These questions are at the edge of my understanding of CTDS methodology. Animals that occur in groups pose a challenge because you cannot be sure of group size from images that capture only a small arc of the area surrounding the camera. Consequently, analysis would proceed with individuals as the detection unit, meaning you would need distances for all individuals in the image.

I don't know how to interpret your second question (what would be the number of observations).

The adjustment for temporal availability would be needed as your diagrams indicate fluctuation in activity over the course of the day.

Perhaps others on the list might provide more insightful answers.
