Hi,
I have distance sampling data from two regions in a flatfile. While running the models using R, I realized that the ds models will give me the density and abundance output for both the regions separately even if I haven't specified region label as a formula. I understand that adding a formula will not fit any adjustment terms to my key function. But I just wanted to understand how these two methods differ (they give nearly the same output).
Also on a related note, if I want to plot the ds model showing the curves separately for each region I should use the model where Region.Label is used within the formula argument right? Somehow running plot on this model doesn't give two separate lines but instead gives one (I had tried it before and it used to work so I am not sure why it's not the case now).

Thank you.

